# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Dávid Péter Kovács et al. (2023). Evaluation of the MACE force field architecture: From medicinal chemistry to materials science.
#   The Journal of Chemical Physics. doi:10.1063/5.0155322  arXiv:2305.14247v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2305.14247v2 (sha256 86959a723502162d...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 617 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/kovacs2023.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the MACE models trained in the paper and their stated
# test errors: three receptive-field variants on each of the seven MD22
# systems (Table I), the 64-0/96-1/192-2 organic models on the ANI-1x
# coupled-cluster subset tested on COMP6 (Table II), HME21 (Table III),
# the M3GNet MPF training set (Table IV), liquid water (Table V) and the
# QM9 U0 task (Table VI). Literature baselines in the same tables are not
# encoded. MACE was introduced in batatia2022; this paper is not its origin.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

