# The paper reports no training-cost or inference-cost figures.

###############################################################################
# Q12 -- Gaps and ambiguities (prose; not triples)
###############################################################################

# - Literature models in Tables I-VI (VisNet-LSRM, sGDML, ANI-1x, GM-NN, NewtonNet, TensorNet, TeaNet, NequIP, M3GNet, BP-NN, REANN and the QM9 models) are baselines and are not encoded.
# - COMP6 errors are total energies in kcal/mol and forces in kcal/mol/A; the models are tested out of distribution, so role external. Water energy errors are per H2O (unit null).
# - Coupled-cluster transfer-learned COMP6 models (biaryl torsion barrier MAE 0.36/0.56/0.83 kcal/mol), revMD17 50/1000-configuration models (from Ref. 18), the CCSD(T) ethanol model and the amorphous-carbon model (force errors only in Fig. 4) have no tabulated energy/force errors here and are not encoded. QM9 tasks other than U0 are molecular properties.
# - The MD22 training-set sizes follow the original MD22 paper and are not restated; the 192-2 water model's channel count is given only by its name.
# - Author affiliations are not encoded (ORCIDs are those deposited with the DOI metadata, source: crossref).
# - Evaluation roles and data, base models, inference timings with their system sizes, and the source location of each value are recorded in the encoding input (artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/kovacs2023.yaml) until the schema has terms for them.

